l":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4069753251/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138922406","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117063#issuecomment-4138922406","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117063","id":4138922406,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc72svGm","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-26T23:10:38Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T23:13:52Z","body":"A line width of `-1` *without* antialiasing uses hardware lines, which have some vendor-specific behavior. Lines *with* antialiasing or with positive widths use software lines (rectangles with feathers for antialiasing). These are 100% consistent across vendors.\n\nThe issue isn't present on Compatibility, as NVIDIA uses Bresenham line drawing on OpenGL (but not Vulkan unless https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/75654 is implemented):\n\n<img width=\"153\" height=\"125\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8eb5ca5e-d535-4acb-877b-0707fa9bd4ca\" />\n\n> Could we make the antialiasing disable specifically for lines with the width of 1 while drawing.\n\nWe probably shouldn't change the existing behavior of negative line widths with antialiasing, as to avoid breaking compatibility with existing projects. However, the current behavior is inconsistent between `draw_line()` (applies antialiasing and switches to software line drawing), while `draw_polyline()` and `draw_dashed_line()` stick to hardware line drawing and ignore the `antialiased` parameter:\n\n<img width=\"118\" height=\"89\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f6da1455-0f18-43ef-b8ab-2eae36fa6f24\" />\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _draw():\n\tdraw_polyline(node_line, Color.WHITE, -1, true)\n\tdraw_polyline(roomline, Color.WHITE, -1, true)\n\tdraw_line(Vector2(-200,0), Vector2(0,-200), Color.RED, -1, true)\n\tdraw_dashed_line(Vector2(-210,0), Vector2(0,-210), Color.GREEN, -1, 2, true, true)\n```\n\nResults in only 3 warnings, not 4:\n\n<img width=\"1060\" height=\"81\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/426a55ef-96a1-4733-ba91-dadc367d1146\" />","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4138922406/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4446569344","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/117063#issuecomment-4446569344","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117063","id":4446569344,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCQlDgA","user":{"login":"Sulca2099","id":171370129,"node_id":"U_kgDOCjbmkQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171370129?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sulca2099","html_url":"https://github.com/Sulca2099","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sulca2099/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sulca2099/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sulca2099/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sulca2099/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sulca2099/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sulca2099/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sulca2099/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sulca2099/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sulca2099/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T01:29:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T01:29:33Z","body":"Thanks for giving me a more in depth view!\nI’m a noob when it comes to game engines.\nMy dad mentioned something about sizing the resolution higher and than downscaling the rendered image, \nBut that can be a negative performance wise I would assume…","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4446569344/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]